# Codebase Conventions

Follow these patterns. Do not introduce new conventions or tools.

## File Structure

```
src/
├── components/atoms/       # Presentational (no getContextStores)
├── components/connected/   # Uses context, selectors, actions
├── context/                # Providers, useReducer, getContextStores
├── actions/                # Action creators
├── reducers/               # Reducers per domain
├── selectors/              # Reselect selectors, map.ts
├── services/               # API via client.server
├── pages/                  # Route-level
├── utils/                  # Pure helpers
└── config/                 # types/, constants
```

## File Naming

- Components: folder `PascalCase` with `index.tsx`
- Styling: `styles.module.less` per component
- Logic/utils: `camelCase.ts` (e.g. `assetManager`, `visibilityFilter`)
- Types: `config/types/*.ts`, re-exported via `config/types/index.ts`

## Imports

- Use **relative paths** (`../../../selectors`, `../../atoms`)
- Order: third-party (react, antd, lodash) → local (selectors, actions, context, utils) → components

## Commands

- `yarn dev` — dev server
- `yarn build` — build
- `yarn lint` — ESLint + tsc (run after changes)
- `yarn test` — Vitest watch
- `yarn test:run` — Vitest single run

## MCP Tool Routing

- Prefer the unified **`devkit`** tool for normal usage in chat.
- Use standalone tools only for Inspector testing/debugging.
- Run **`pre_pr_quality_gate`** before **`repo_open_pr`**.

## Stack (typical layered SPA)

- React, TypeScript, Vite
- Ant Design; **antd `Form`** for forms (not proprietary dynamic-form packages)
- LESS modules (`styles.module.less`), reselect, react-router
- ESLint per project config

